course: dictionary
lesson: 13097
title: Words for people who sell things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a person and a place at the same time. A fishmonger is a person, and the fishmonger's is their shop. «Mum bought cod at the fishmonger's on Saturday.» The apostrophe shows the shop belongs to the fishmonger.
explain: Look at the words around the new word to find its meaning. «The fishmonger cut the salmon into neat steaks.» Cutting salmon and selling it tells you the fishmonger works with fresh fish, not meat or bread. Try the meaning in the sentence: a person who sells fish fits, so you have it.
explain: Compare it with words that sound alike. A butcher sells meat, a greengrocer sells fruit and vegetables, and an ironmonger sells tools. Each word tells you what the shop sells, so when you learn one, you can work out the others.
fact: A fishmonger is a person who sells fresh fish and seafood.
fact: The fishmonger's is the shop where fish is sold.
fact: A fishmonger often cleans and cuts fish for customers.
fact: In the past, fishmongers worked at busy markets, such as Billingsgate in London.
fact: Similar words: «butcher» (meat), «greengrocer» (fruit and vegetables), «ironmonger» (tools).
exercise: «The fishmonger cut the salmon into neat steaks.» Who cut the salmon? | The postman | The baker | The farmer | *The fishmonger
exercise: «We bought prawns at the fishmonger's on Saturday.» Where did they buy the prawns? | At the ironmonger's | At the greengrocer's | At the butcher's | *At the fishmonger's
exercise: Which shop sells fruit and vegetables? | Ironmonger | Butcher | *Greengrocer | Fishmonger
test: What is a fishmonger? | A fish with a long tail | *A person who sells fresh fish and seafood | A person who sells bread | A kind of small boat
test: «The fishmonger shouted the prices at the busy market.» Which famous market in London were fishmongers known for? | *Billingsgate | Oxford Street | Buckingham Palace | Hyde Park
exam: «The fishmonger's shop smelt of the sea.» In this sentence, what is the fishmonger's? | *The shop where fish is sold | The sea | A fish with a long tail | A market stall for vegetables
